20 0 obj
<< /A 314 0 R /Alt (Panel a shows a tissue section with very few brown-stained cells, indicating minimal marker expression. Panel b displays moderate brown staining along cell membranes in some areas, suggesting intermediate expression. Panel c features extensive, intense brown staining throughout, indicative of high marker expression in the tissue.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 15 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
21 0 obj
<< /A 315 0 R /Alt (Panel a shows a histology tissue section with a digital pathology user interface on the right, while panel b shows the same section with nuclei marked in blue, a yellow region of interest overlaid, and statistical data displayed.) /K 1 /P 8 0 R /Pg 15 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
22 0 obj
<< /A 316 0 R /Alt (Scatter plot comparing uPath TPS percentage \(x-axis\) and Pathologist TPS percentage \(y-axis\) with many blue data points and a diagonal line showing strong positive linear correlation across the full range of values.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 16 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
23 0 obj
<< /A 317 0 R /Alt (Two pie charts compare agreement between AI and pathologist assessments. Left chart shows ninety-four percent unchanged PD-L1 category, six percent reclassified. Right chart shows ninety-five point two percent unchanged PD-L1 status, four point eight percent reclassified.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 17 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
24 0 obj
<< /A 318 0 R /Alt (Bar chart comparing median differences in TPS percentage by expression group, showing values of 0.2 percentage points for TPS less than 1 percent, 4.4 percentage points for TPS one to forty-nine percent, and 1.95 percentage points for TPS greater than or equal to fifty percent.) /K 1 /P 8 0 R /Pg 17 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
